WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:05.622
Now let's practice text normalization and fallback
values The goal

00:00:05.648 --> 00:00:10.495
is to display a preferred language If the language
contains useful text

00:00:10.611 --> 00:00:15.495
keep it If it is null empty or only spaces display
Language

00:00:15.521 --> 00:00:19.580
not recorded The query first uses B trim and null if
to

00:00:19.593 --> 00:00:26.184
normalize the text Then coalesce provides the final
fallback Run

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:30.127
the example in the browser and compare preferred
language with language display

00:00:31.646 --> 00:00:35.977
You can also click Copy and run the query in pgAdmin
Try

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:41.080
to identify which records actually needed the
fallback This pattern is useful

00:00:41.106 --> 00:00:46.724
far beyond this example Whenever user-entered text
may contain blank or whitespace-only

00:00:46.737 --> 00:00:51.402
values normalizing before applying business logic
makes the result much more reliable
